{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/638821-deva-corporation-endowment","id":638821,"title":"Deva Corporation Endowment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-24T22:44:15-07:00","id":638821,"title":"Deva Corporation Endowment?","content":"So I'm tinkering with an India setting for HtV, and it obviously stands to reason that the Deva Corporation would be one of the dominant indigenously based Conspiracies. I'm curious if anyone has any ideas for unique Endowment tech for them that isn't just a rehash of VALKYRIE's Armory, or cybernetic looking Thaumatechnology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T02:19:22-07:00","id":638884,"title":"","content":"I've write a quick and dirty version of Endowments for them, based around Dread Powers-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Deva Corporation- Luminous Advancements (0-00000)</b><br /> being a part of a great Infrastructure, the hunter may channel its might through her and gain special Advancements for her used. In order to use the Endowment, the hunter must first &quot;tune&quot; to a certain Infrastructure, which requires rolling Endowment+Occult. Success means that the hunter may gain a number of Dread Powers equal to their dots in the Endowments, which are decided by the ST as powers which may advance the goal of the Infrastructure. The hunter stays tuned to the Infrastructure for one day per dot in the Endowment, although she may &quot;tune off&quot; at any moment. She may not be tuned to more than one Infrastructure at a time. The Dread Powers manifested by the hunter are usually manifested in the form of mechanical items or technological devices which may be operated only by the hands of the hunter. Exceptional Success means the duration is doubled. Failure gives a -1 modifier to any roll for tuning to the same Infrastructure in the same day. Dramatic Failure means an angel would be sent to investigate the &quot;security breach&quot; and deal with it. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T02:38:23-07:00","id":638888,"title":"","content":"Honestly, while I know that was the suggestion in mortal remains, but I'd go in a different direction entirely.<br /> <br /> For something that hasn't been done before, since the G-M gives out supernatural merits, perhaps they have &quot;psitech&quot; that boosts supernatural merits? Like a visor that gives a boost to aura sight, or a PK gun that makes psychokinesis far more dangerous.<br /> <br /> Or maybe they take demonic gadgets and take them a part, and have figured out how to put them back together well enough for endowment level gadgetry?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T14:20:18-07:00","id":639463,"title":"","content":"I like the idea StSword - sort of playing off the idea that Deva Hunters are going to be Stigmatics, and the corp has refined that further through tech. How would you handle that in a Hunter game purchase wise. I suppose Second Edition does put psychic merits in the core, so it can just be assumed that a player who buys these Endowments is also going to buy some psychic ability. Alternatively, it wouldn't be out of line to just make them free-with-purchase. If the player buys &quot;pyrokinesis enhancement&quot; gear, they character gets the basic pyrokinesis merit for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-25T23:42:49-07:00","id":639892,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well just spitballing here, but one idea is that the deva &quot;enhanced psychics&quot; can buy supernatural merits as endowments (merits are merits after all), and put them through the endowment creation process for the boosts.<br /> <br /> Take the idea of the aura vision visor for example, perhaps it allows the deva agent to read more than one aura at a time, or they can add &quot;sense monster&quot; so that the deva agent can automatically detect a certain type of supernatural by their aura.<br /> <br /> A biofeedback suit for biokinesis might add healing or enhanced attribute.<br /> <br /> A PK gun might allow one to do agg damage, or hit more than person at a time through autofire.<br /> <br /> I suppose if one wants, considering how merits work in second edition, you could keep them separate. So an agent with psychometry can then buy features and frailties for it as the psitech gadget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}